For the following PHPUnit tests, make sure you have the Board model, BoardController, and any other necessary classes set up in your project.

Continue adding tests in the existing BoardTest.php file:

```php
<?php

// ... (include the previous test code here)

class BoardTest extends TestCase
{
    // ... (include the previous tests here)

    /** @test */
    public function it_can_delete_a_board()
    {
        $user = User::factory()->create();
        $workspace = Workspace::factory()->create(['user_id' => $user->id]);
        $board = Board::factory()->create([
            'workspace_id' => $workspace->id,
            'name' => 'Sample Board',
        ]);

        $response = $this->actingAs($user)->deleteJson("/api/boards/{$board->id}");

        $response->assertStatus(204); // No Content

        $this->assertDatabaseMissing('boards', [
            'id' => $board->id,
        ]);
    }

    /** @test */  
    public function it_prompts_confirmation_before_deleting_board()
    {
        // This test cannot be implemented using PHPUnit directly, as PHPUnit is a server-side testing framework
        // and cannot interact with client-side browser functionalities such as prompts or alerts.
        // To test browser interactions like prompts, consider using a browser testing tool like Laravel Dusk.
        $this->assertTrue(true);
    }

    /** @test */
    public function it_restricts_deleting_boards_for_unauthorized_users()
    {
        $user = User::factory()->create();
        $workspace = Workspace::factory()->create(['user_id' => $user->id]);
        $board = Board::factory()->create([
            'workspace_id' => $workspace->id,
            'name' => 'Sample Board',
        ]);

        $unauthorizedUser = User::factory()->create(); // New unauthorized user

        $response = $this->actingAs($unauthorizedUser)->deleteJson("/api/boards/{$board->id}");

        $response->assertStatus(403); // Forbidden
    }
}
```

The tests above will cover scenarios such as:
- Deleting a board with valid data, ensuring it's removed from the database.
- Displaying a confirmation prompt before deleting a board (this cannot be tested directly with PHPUnit, instead, you may use a browser testing tool like Laravel Dusk).
- Verifying restrictions on deleting board details for unauthorized users, expecting a 403 Forbidden status code.

Be sure to adjust the paths, factories, and any other dependencies according to your project's specific configuration.
